  'ln.metTorah': "already in “Torah words”: {n}",
  'ln.seoTitle': "Learn Hebrew — the language of the Torah and Prophets, free",
  'ln.seoLead': "The Holy Tongue (Lashon HaKodesh) step by step: the alef-bet, the words of the Torah by weekly portion and all 5215 words of the Prophets and Writings, the most frequent first. 5-minute lessons, a test, free — for kids and adults.",
  'ln.seoShort': "Learn Hebrew — the language of the Torah and the Prophets",
  'ln.seoHow': "Like Duolingo: a lesson takes 5 minutes and brings 5–6 new words. Pick the meaning, match the pairs, build the word from its letters, put the words of a verse in order, find the missing letter. A mistake comes back at the end of the lesson, reviews make the words stick, and a test lets you pass a whole unit at once. You don’t need to know Hebrew: if you don’t know the letters, the site names them and shows how the word is read.",
  'ln.seoStart': "Start a lesson",
  'ln.seoAbcH': "Letters: the Hebrew alphabet in two units",
  'ln.seoAbcP': "First the 22 letters and the 5 final forms: what a letter looks like, its name, its sound and its number. Letters that look alike (ב and כ, ד and ר, ה and ח) stand side by side so you don’t mix them up.",
  'ln.seoTorahH': "The language of the Torah: words of the weekly portions",
  'ln.seoTorahP': "The words of the Torah from our lessons — a portion at a time: Bereishit, Noach, Lech Lecha, Vayera… With translation and pictures; the words you learn also count in the “Torah words” game.",
  'ln.seoTanakhH': "The language of the Prophets: all 5215 words of Tanakh, the most frequent first",
  'ln.seoTanakhP': "For teens and adults — levels of 50 words of the Prophets and Writings by frequency: the first 500 words are 80% of the text. Words already in “My words” don’t have to be learned again; the ones you pass go there for review.",
  'ln.seoFaqH': "Questions and answers",
  'ln.seoQ1': "How do I start learning the language of the Torah if I don’t know Hebrew?",
  'ln.seoA1': "Start with the letters: two short units and you know them all. Then the words of the Torah by weekly portion. Every word comes with its translation — and, if you chose “I don’t know the letters”, with how it is read.",
  'ln.seoQ2': "How is the language of the Torah and the Prophets different from modern Hebrew?",
  'ln.seoA2': "It is the Holy Tongue — Lashon HaKodesh, the language of the Torah, the Prophets and the Writings. Many words are the same as in modern Hebrew, but here you learn the words of the text of Tanakh itself — in their basic form, with the root and an example verse.",
  'ln.seoQ3': "How many words do I need to read the Prophets?",
  'ln.seoA3': "The 100 most frequent words are more than half of the text of the Prophets and Writings, 500 are 80%, 1000 almost 90%, 1500 are 93%, 2000 are 95%, 2500 are 97%, 3000 are 98%.",
  'ln.seoQ4': "Is it free?",
  'ln.seoA4': "Yes: every lesson is free, in Russian, English and German. You only need to sign in with your email (no password) — and your progress is kept on all your devices.",
  'reading.seoTitle': "Tehillim online: read the whole book with us in 102 minutes",
  'reading.seoShort': "Fluent Tehillim reading",
  'reading.seoLead': "Read the whole book of Tehillim (Psalms) with us in 102 minutes! All 150 chapters in Hebrew with vowels, a reader’s recording for every chapter, the word lit up as it is read, and any speed from 0.5× to 3.5×. Free, no sign-up.",
  'reading.seoHow': "Turn on the recording: the word being read lights up in the text, and your eyes follow the voice. Start slowly, at 0.75× or 1×, and as the letters grow familiar, speed up — that is how reading becomes fast and confident. Fell behind or ran ahead? Tap the word you are reading, and the highlight goes on from there. Cantillation marks and a large font are a tick away.",
  'reading.seoStart': "Read Tehillim",
  'reading.seoTimeH': "How long the whole book takes",
  'reading.seoTimeP': "All 150 chapters in the recording — {words} words, about {total} at normal speed. The faster you read, the shorter the way:",
  'reading.seoTimeRow': "{rate} — {time}",
  'reading.seoWaysH': "How to read: the portion of the day, by days of the week, for your dear ones",
  'reading.seoWaysP': "“Tehillim for today” — the portion for the day of the Hebrew month: the whole book in a month. “By days of the week” — from Sunday (chapters 1–29) to Shabbat (120–150): the whole book in a week. “My chapters” — your own list of chapters with the names of those you read for (kept only in this browser). And “All Tehillim” — any of the 150 chapters.",
  'reading.seoChaptersH': "All 150 chapters of Tehillim",
  'reading.seoFaqH': "Frequently asked questions",
  'reading.seoQ1': "Can I read the whole book of Tehillim in one day?",
  'reading.seoA1': "Yes. With the recording at 3.5×, the whole book takes about 102 minutes; at 3×, about two hours; at 2×, about three. Many read all of Tehillim on special occasions — on a birthday or for the recovery of someone dear.",
  'reading.seoQ2': "Do I need to know Hebrew?",
  'reading.seoA2': "You need to recognize the letters and vowels — understanding every word is not required. If the letters are still new to you, start with “The letters in 5 minutes” and the Holy Tongue lessons on this site.",
  'reading.seoQ3': "Which portion do I read today?",
  'reading.seoA3': "The portion of the day follows the day of the Hebrew month, as is the custom: on the 1st, chapters 1–9, and so on — by the end of the month, the whole book. The site opens today’s portion by itself; you can also choose the division by days of the week.",
  'reading.seoQ4': "Is it free?",
  'reading.seoA4': "Yes: the text, the recordings of all 150 chapters and every setting are free, with no sign-up, in Russian, English and German.",
  'reading.seoHomeLinks': "Portion of the day · by days of the week · all 150 chapters",
