  'tanakh.seo.neviim.q1': "Which books are in the Prophets (Nevi'im)?",
  'tanakh.seo.neviim.a1': "{books} books, {chapters} chapters: from {first} to {last} — the Former Prophets (Joshua, Judges, Samuel, Kings), Isaiah, Jeremiah, Ezekiel and the Twelve. They are read in order, a passage every study day.",
  'tanakh.seo.ketuvim.q1': "Which books are in the Writings (Ketuvim)?",
  'tanakh.seo.ketuvim.a1': "{books} books, {chapters} chapters: from {first} to {last} — Tehillim, Mishlei, Job, the five scrolls (Song of Songs, Ruth, Eichah, Kohelet, Esther), Daniel, Ezra, Nehemiah and Chronicles. They are read in order, a passage every study day.",
  'tanakh.seo.q2': "Is it free?",
  'tanakh.seo.a2': "Yes: no subscription and no ads. You sign in with a code sent to your email, no password; the first month everything is open even without signing in.",
  'tanakh.seo.q3': "Which English translation is used?",
  'tanakh.seo.a3': "JPS 1985 (“Tanakh: The Holy Scriptures”, Jewish Publication Society, CC BY-NC) for every verse of every book; the two verses missing from it (Joshua 21:36–37) follow JPS 1917. Next to it — the Hebrew text with vowels.",
  'tanakh.seo.q4': "Is there Rashi and Metzudat David in English?",
  'tanakh.seo.a4': "Rashi — yes, in English for every book (the Metsudah and Judaica Press translations). Metzudat David is translated into English by the project a week ahead, ready through {until}; after that date it is shown in Hebrew until the translation is ready.",
  'tanakh.seo.q5': "How long does a passage take?",
  'tanakh.seo.a5': "Usually about {min} minutes: the Hebrew read aloud, the English translation and Metzudat David. The time of each passage is shown above it; without the commentary it is shorter.",
  'tanakh.seo.q6': "Can I start at any time?",
  'tanakh.seo.a6': "Yes. The cycle runs {start} – {end} ({days} study days, no Shabbat or festivals), but “at my own pace” starts from the first passage and always opens the first one you have not read. For every book read, the Niflaot Academy gives an “Expert in the book” certificate.",
  'academy.hemshech': "Chassidut: Hemshech Samech-Vav",
  'academy.hemshechNote': "A certificate for a discourse — when all its passages are read (100%): mark “I’ve read it” under each. If the questions on all these passages are passed with at least {pass}% too, the certificate shows points. Here — the discourses whose study has begun.",
